// Module c-pediatric: what a general medical student or resident should recognize in child
// neurology. Developmental domains, red flags, and regression; the floppy infant (central versus
// peripheral, including spinal muscular atrophy); simple and complex febrile seizures, childhood
// absence epilepsy, and infantile spasms; and recognition of neurofibromatosis type 1, tuberous
// sclerosis complex, and Duchenne muscular dystrophy, with the role of genetic testing and
// counseling. Treatment doses are deliberately left out.

